But we'll settle on looks.

253
00:10:22,650 --> 00:10:26,160
But remember that imagination
is as important as knowledge.

254
00:10:26,150 --> 00:10:27,650
-Hm?
-Yes, imagination.

255
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:28,660
-Ah.
-Oh.

256
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:31,160
-And this you possess by nature.
-Mm, neat.

257
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:33,160
The next most important thing...

258
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,170
-...is prudence.
-Is peanut butter.

259
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:38,660
But this man learns only
with the passage of time.

260
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:40,170
More than you.

261
00:10:40,170 --> 00:10:43,670
I've waited until now
to show you my discovery.

262
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:46,670
A rear-view mirror?

263
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:49,180
-Stronger than dirt.
-What is it?

264
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:50,680
It is everything and nothing.

265
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:53,680
Uh, could you be
a little more vague, please?

266
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,190
It is life and death.

267
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:57,180
Goodness...

268
00:10:57,690 --> 00:11:02,690
-And badness.
...riches and poverty. And evil.

269
00:11:02,690 --> 00:11:04,700
-It's boss!
-Neat.

270
00:11:05,690 --> 00:11:07,690
It all depends on Man.

271
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:10,700
-What are Man's options?
-What Man does with it.

272
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:11,200
Oh.

273
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,700
-Okay.
-Then, it might...

274
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,710
-[ Window-wiping noise ]
-...might be a weapon.

275
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:16,700
-Exactly.
-Mm-hm.

276
00:11:16,710 --> 00:11:18,210
And like all weapons,

277
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:20,710
it must be kept
away from ambitious men.

278
00:11:20,710 --> 00:11:22,710
-Ah.
-And Nazis.

279
00:11:22,710 --> 00:11:24,220
But, Father, how can I save it?

280
00:11:24,210 --> 00:11:26,210
No, daughter, your hands
are too weak.

281
00:11:26,210 --> 00:11:27,210
You'll get fingerprints
all over it.

282
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:29,720
Zor's thirst for power...

283
00:11:30,220 --> 00:11:31,720
...is too strong.

284
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:33,720
He's heading south
with his henchmen.

285
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,730
I know.

286
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,720
I can see myself in there.

287
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,720
But he would never dare
to enter our territory.

288
00:11:39,230 --> 00:11:42,730
I wonder if it's worth the risk
of counting on that.

289
00:11:42,730 --> 00:11:43,730
Or the risk of acting.

290
00:11:44,230 --> 00:11:46,230
But, Father, you taught me
that science is always a risk.

291
00:11:46,230 --> 00:11:49,730
Ah, but a man of science
takes a calculated risk.

292
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,740
Mm.

293
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:53,240
Science is only a means,
one of many, to obtain...

294
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,750
-There is also fan dancing.
-Ooh.

295
00:11:59,750 --> 00:12:02,750
What do you,
the viewers at home, think?

296
00:12:02,750 --> 00:12:06,260
I am now too old
for so great a responsibility.

297
00:12:06,250 --> 00:12:08,750
And for such flashy jewelry.

298
00:12:10,260 --> 00:12:12,760
What do you intend doing?

299
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:15,270
To protect a thing
of such great import...

300
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:16,260
tance!

301
00:12:16,260 --> 00:12:18,260
There is only one man.

302
00:12:19,770 --> 00:12:21,270
Ator.

303
00:12:21,770 --> 00:12:23,770
-But he's a baby.
-Ator is the son of Torren.

304
00:12:24,770 --> 00:12:27,270
He was born during the tenebrous
era of the Spider Kingdom.

305
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:29,280
Wow, everybody did drugs then,
I guess.

306
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:31,780
--in the service of Dakkar
and his spotted high priest,

307
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:34,790
-...were sent out to--
hese must be Ator's home movies.

308
00:12:34,780 --> 00:12:37,780
--former high priest carried off
the infant Ator to safety.

309
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:39,790
Uh, this is the part of the film

310
00:12:39,790 --> 00:12:41,790
we like to call
"She Had to Ask".

311
00:12:41,790 --> 00:12:42,790
--the black knights--
-Yep.

312
00:12:42,790 --> 00:12:44,300
ho constantly scoured the land--
-Uh-huh.

313
00:12:44,790 --> 00:12:46,790
--sacrificial victims
of the Spider God.

314
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:47,800
Spider God, uh-huh.

315
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,300
Sweeping down upon the village
where Ator, now a young man--

316
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:51,800
Yeah.

317
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:54,810
--black knights badly wounded
him and carried off Sunya,

318
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:55,800
his young bride.

319
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,300
-Gettin' all this?
-Say.

320
00:12:57,310 --> 00:12:58,310
Whoa.

321
00:12:59,310 --> 00:13:01,310
-As Ator nursed his wounds...
-I nursed a scotch.

322
00:13:01,310 --> 00:13:03,310
...he swore to rescue Sunya

323
00:13:03,310 --> 00:13:05,820
and crush the iron-handed rule
of Dakkar.

324
00:13:06,310 --> 00:13:07,310
Who?

325
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,320
Griba...

326
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:11,320
Son of Flogmug, Keeper
of the Seven Keys of Pentoozler.

327
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:14,830
...encouraged Ator
and taught him the martial arts.

328
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:15,820
And Marshall Crenshaw.

329
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:18,830
Marshall Tucker.

330
00:13:18,830 --> 00:13:20,830
ings are movin' real fast. Whoo.
-Yeah.

331
00:13:21,830 --> 00:13:23,330
-Enjoy it while it lasts.
-Hey, Jean Kasem.

332
00:13:23,830 --> 00:13:26,840
When Ator was deemed ready
to set out on his mission,

333
00:13:27,340 --> 00:13:28,840
-...Griba revealed-...
-Say. Nice.

334
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:33,840
...noble heritage and consigned
to him the Sword of Torren.

335
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:35,850
No, the shroud of Turin.
Sheesh.

336
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:38,340
Geez. Tolkien
couldn't follow this plot.

337
00:13:38,850 --> 00:13:40,850
- [ Snores ]
-Not enough dwarves.

338
00:13:50,630 --> 00:13:54,130
-It's the Wango the Tango!
-Whoo!

339
00:13:54,630 --> 00:13:56,130
Get down.

340
00:13:57,630 --> 00:14:00,130
Before Ator could conquer
the Spider Kingdom,

341
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:03,140
he came under the spell
of the beautiful witch Indun.

342
00:14:03,140 --> 00:14:04,140
Ooh, Cher at the funhouse.

343
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:05,640
A thousand-year-old
enchantress...

344
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:07,140
-Yick.
-Ugh.

345
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:10,650
...who called forth a horrible
army of walking dead. Of slaves.

346
00:14:11,150 --> 00:14:12,650
It's Aztec mommy!

347
00:14:13,650 --> 00:14:14,650
Ooh, how graphic.

348
00:14:15,150 --> 00:14:18,660
-Wow.
-Check me out, I'm not half bad.

349
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:22,150
--captured the glistening
charmed shield of Murdor.

350
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,160
And the secret decoder ring.

351
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:29,170
Oh, come on. Those moon boots
went out in the '70s.

352
00:14:31,170 --> 00:14:33,170
At last, Ator confronted Dakkar.

353
00:14:33,170 --> 00:14:35,170
Played by Tommy Chong.

354
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:36,670
...and his gruesome
deformed warriors

355
00:14:36,670 --> 00:14:38,180
in a battle to the death.

356
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:41,680
Oh, he's been gonged.

357
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:47,180
Whoa.

358
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:49,690
Aided by the incredibly potent
shield of Murdor...

359
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:52,680
-And its free prize inside.
-...the malicious priest...

360
00:14:53,190 --> 00:14:56,690
...then had to kill Griba, who
had revealed his evil designs

361
00:14:56,690 --> 00:14:59,200
for obtaining power
by using Ator as his pawn.

362
00:14:59,190 --> 00:15:00,190
Then he broke for a light lunch.

363
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,200
After rescuing Sunya...

364
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:04,200
Ator faced the immense,
hideous spider itself...

365
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,700
Ee.

366
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:06,700
...and plunged
the Sword of Torren

367
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:07,710
into the grisly creature's body.

368
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:10,700
He'd never killed, uh,
that big a puppet before.

369
00:15:10,710 --> 00:15:12,710
When the Spider God was killed,

370
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:14,710
the forces of blackest evil
were unleashed--

371
00:15:14,710 --> 00:15:17,210
Uh, objects in shield are
smaller than they appear.

372
00:15:17,710 --> 00:15:19,710
--forth its molten magma
in anger.

373
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:24,220
Then he worked out
on the charismatic solo flex

374
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:25,720
of Zontar 13.

375
00:15:28,220 --> 00:15:29,720
[ Grunts ]

376
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:32,730
Now rest. You deserve it.
[ Chuckles ]

377
00:15:33,730 --> 00:15:37,740
Later, when Sunya died, Ator
retired to the eastern land,

378
00:15:37,730 --> 00:15:40,230
where he lives
in the company of Thong,

379
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:42,240
an Oriental warrior and savior.

380
00:15:42,240 --> 00:15:44,740
Played here by Jimmy Carl Black
of The Mothers of Invention.

381
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:48,250
[ Sharp scratching noise ]

382
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,740
-Ooh, I hate that.
-That's enough for now, Thong.

383
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:52,750
Uh, scratching, that is.

384
00:15:53,750 --> 00:15:56,250
You know, that exercise works.
You were right.

385
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:58,760
-I can feel it here.
-Wait, where's my shirt?

386
00:15:58,750 --> 00:16:00,250
The muscles are stronger.

387
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:01,760
Yeah.

388
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:03,760
-Are we still in a flashback?
-Ah--

389
00:16:03,760 --> 00:16:05,260
-I think so.
-I don't know.

390
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:06,760
[ French accent ] Cato.

391
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:14,270
Whoa.

392
00:16:15,770 --> 00:16:16,770
You get to be
a teppanyaki chef.

393
00:16:16,770 --> 00:16:17,780
Yeah.

394
00:16:17,770 --> 00:16:20,770
-Am I still usin' that old move?
- [ Chuckles ]

395
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:25,780
Ha, ha, hey, kiba!

396
00:16:27,780 --> 00:16:29,780
You should see him
with vegetables.

397
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:30,780
Okay.

398
00:16:32,790 --> 00:16:35,290
Oh, not done yet. Hai!
[ Slashing noises ]

399
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:41,290
Then they do improv exercises.

400
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:42,800
Whoo.

401
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:45,800
Align the vertebrae,
and release.

402
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:47,300
And break.

403
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:48,310
Shake it out.

404
00:16:49,300 --> 00:16:50,800
There.
That'll do.

405
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:52,310
Now, where was I?

406
00:16:52,310 --> 00:16:54,310
Charmed shield,
incredibly potent--

407
00:16:54,310 --> 00:16:55,810
-Father?
- [ Startled gasp ]

408
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:56,810
Yes, my dear?

409
00:16:58,810 --> 00:16:59,810
-Tell me.
-Again?

410
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:01,810
-No!
-No, no, no!

411
00:17:03,820 --> 00:17:05,320
[ Sighs ]

412
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:06,820
All right.

413
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:08,830
Daughter...

414
00:17:09,320 --> 00:17:10,820
you know you're
the only person...

415
00:17:10,830 --> 00:17:12,330
Oh, I know what's gonna happen.

416
00:17:12,330 --> 00:17:13,830
...who could recognize
the urgency of my cause.

417
00:17:13,830 --> 00:17:14,830
Mm-hm.

418
00:17:14,830 --> 00:17:17,330
But I can't leave you
at a time like this.

419
00:17:17,330 --> 00:17:18,840
During a flashback.

420
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:21,830
Dear, you will find
with the passing of time

421
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:25,340
that you can't always have
what you want.

422
00:17:25,340 --> 00:17:26,340
But if you try sometimes,

423
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:28,350
you just might find you get
what you need.

424
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:29,840
But you're the only one I have.

425
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,340
-You and the duck.
-My dear Mila.

426
00:17:34,850 --> 00:17:36,850
You don't have to worry
about my safety.

427
00:17:36,850 --> 00:17:39,860
A sly old fox like me knows
how to take care of himself.

428
00:17:39,850 --> 00:17:41,850
These are things a man
has to learn.

429
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:42,860
Quit shakin' me, Dad.

430
00:17:42,860 --> 00:17:46,360
And goes on repeating
for the rest of life,

431
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,370
unfortunately.

432
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,860
-What?
-Stately Wayne Manor.

433
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:51,870
What's Wayne Manor?

434
00:17:51,870 --> 00:17:54,370
Oh, that's where Batman
lived before he, uh, became

435
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:55,870
The Dark Knight
in those comic books.

436
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:57,880
Oh, they're not comic books,
they're graphic novels.

437
00:17:57,870 --> 00:17:58,870
-Oh.
-Come on.

438
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:03,380
Music
by The Super Mario Brothers.

439
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:04,380
[ Effort grunts ]

440
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:06,880
- [ Horse whinnies ]
- [ Effort grunts ]

441
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,880
[ Grunts ]
Quit pushin' back there. Ooh.

442
00:18:10,890 --> 00:18:12,890
Keep your swords down,
you're inside now.

443
00:18:14,890 --> 00:18:18,400
That city's supposed to be
around here somewhere.

444
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:20,390
-Let's see.
-Follow me!

445
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:22,900
-We are.
-Uh, we're trying.

446
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,900
-Which--? Oh, that--? Oh, okay.
-This way!

447
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:30,900
- [ Clearing throats ]
- [ Whistles ]

448
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:31,910
[ Shouting ]

449
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:34,410
Run outside and see
what the trouble is, quickly!

450
00:18:34,910 --> 00:18:36,410
-But you--
-Go, I told you.

451
00:18:37,410 --> 00:18:39,420
-And be careful.
-Huh?

452
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:42,910
[ Excited breath ]
Later. Later.

453
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:44,920
[ Whistles ]

454
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:46,420
Well, better 86 the hooch.

455
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,920
A little nip won't hurt.
[ Hums ]

456
00:18:50,430 --> 00:18:51,930
[ Attack yells ]

457
00:18:53,930 --> 00:18:56,430
Use the handrails.
Safety on the stairway.

458
00:18:56,930 --> 00:18:59,440
-Hey, wait for me.
-Me, too.

459
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:02,930
Hey, wait up. Hey,
I found some funny wet clay.

460
00:19:05,440 --> 00:19:08,450
-It's raining men, hallelujah.
-Whew.

461
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,440
[ Fighting noises ]

462
00:19:12,450 --> 00:19:13,450
Yee-hoo!

463
00:19:15,950 --> 00:19:17,960
-Dad, tell me another story.
-Zor is here.

464
00:19:18,950 --> 00:19:21,450
I should have realized
the time was so close.

465
00:19:21,460 --> 00:19:22,960
I've read the script.

466
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:25,960
You must ride due east
and try to reach Ator.

467
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:27,970
The road's long and hard...

468
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,960
[ Pneumatic
tube-sucking noises ]

469
00:19:30,470 --> 00:19:32,970
When you seem to have reached
the ends of the earth--

470
00:19:32,970 --> 00:19:33,970
Ask for Earl.

471
00:19:34,470 --> 00:19:35,970
--and it seems
that nature herself

472
00:19:35,970 --> 00:19:39,480
declines to accompany you
any further on your journey,

473
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:42,470
then you will have reached
the domain of Ator.

474
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,980
Canada?

475
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:45,980
How can you ask me
to do this now?

476
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:48,490
It is not for myself that I ask,
Mila,

477
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:49,980
but for the welfare
of all mankind.

478
00:19:49,980 --> 00:19:50,980
Ah.

479
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:51,990
Go.

480
00:19:51,990 --> 00:19:53,990
Take a sweater.
And be back by 10!

481
00:19:55,490 --> 00:19:56,490
Hi.

482
00:19:56,990 --> 00:19:58,500
[ Struggling noises ]

483
00:19:58,490 --> 00:19:59,490
Huh?

484
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:01,990
-That's my spice rack!
-Aw.

485
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
[ Groans ]

486
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,010
-Dad?
-Poor guy.

487
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Stop!

488
00:20:11,010 --> 00:20:12,510
-Huh?
-Hm?

489
00:20:13,010 --> 00:20:16,010
How dare you lay hands on him,
you mangy dogs?

490
00:20:16,010 --> 00:20:19,520
All of you put together are not
worth this man's little finger.

491
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:21,510
And I mean that from
the bottom of my heart.

492
00:20:21,520 --> 00:20:23,020
Out!

493
00:20:30,530 --> 00:20:31,530
Help me.

494
00:20:34,030 --> 00:20:36,530
You know, that hat has
a slimming effect on you.

495
00:20:36,530 --> 00:20:40,540
I thought that among
your many virtues...

496
00:20:40,540 --> 00:20:41,540
Mm-hm?

497
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:44,040
...the first I'd find
was forgiveness.

498
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:45,540
Oh, I'm sorry. I-

499
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:49,050
Perhaps I've not yet
quite acquired...

500
00:20:50,550 --> 00:20:51,550
total control...

501
00:20:51,550 --> 00:20:53,050
-Of--?
-...over myself.

502
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:58,060
Come, they are only
petty soldiers.

503
00:20:58,550 --> 00:21:02,050
They can't approach
your exalted level.

504
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:03,560
Oh, thanks,
but now's no time to kiss up.

505
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:07,060
My life comes to an end,
all levels, I would say.

506
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:08,570
Really?

507
00:21:08,560 --> 00:21:13,560
Now... for my own part,
I fail to see why during life...

508
00:21:13,570 --> 00:21:14,570
Uh-huh?

509
00:21:15,570 --> 00:21:18,080
...we create artificial
distinctions between ourselves.

510
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:19,570
-Mm-hm.
-Hm.

511
00:21:19,570 --> 00:21:21,070
Because all men
are born equal.

512
00:21:21,080 --> 00:21:24,080
Oh, let me get a pencil,
I wanna write that one down.

513
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:25,580
Makes me sick.

514
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:28,590
I've become more
and more certain

515
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:30,580
that my little visit here...

516
00:21:30,590 --> 00:21:33,090
-Mm-hm?
-...was fully justified

517
00:21:33,090 --> 00:21:35,090
and will be
extremely profitable.

518
00:21:35,090 --> 00:21:37,090
You can write it off
on your taxes.

519
00:21:37,090 --> 00:21:39,100
-Mm-hm.
-Do you imply...

520
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:41,090
-Mm-hm?
-...that you are a conqueror...

521
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:42,100
Mm-hm?

522
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:45,100
...who claims
the spoils of victory?

523
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:47,100
Or are you...

524
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:48,610
...a common...

525
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:50,100
...thief?

526
00:21:51,110 --> 00:21:52,110
Oh, Geez, this has more pauses
than a Pinter play.

527
00:21:52,610 --> 00:21:54,610
[ Laughs ]

528
00:21:54,610 --> 00:21:57,610
- [ Laughs ]
-Oh, observational humor.

529
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:00,610
God, I love Seinfeld.

530
00:22:00,620 --> 00:22:02,620
-Oh, we gotta get outta here.
-Let's go.

531
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:09,130
In this case, let's just say
I'm an unexpected guest.

532
00:22:18,130 --> 00:22:19,630
-Ooh! Ooh!
- [ Laughs ]

533
00:22:19,630 --> 00:22:20,630
Ah! Ah! Too tight.

534
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:21,640
-Oh, oh.
-Whoa, there.

535
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,140
I don't know, Joel.
I don't think this is for me.

536
00:22:24,140 --> 00:22:25,640
Whoops, I lost it.
Uh, it's okay.

537
00:22:25,640 --> 00:22:26,640
Yeah.

538
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:27,640
What do you mean?

539
00:22:28,140 --> 00:22:29,640
You look fantastic.
I could eat ya up.

540
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:31,140
Oh, and I could bite
that big toe.

541
00:22:31,150 --> 00:22:34,150
-Ooh hoo hoo.
-Hey, now, quit clowning.

542
00:22:34,150 --> 00:22:36,650
You know, what we're gonna do
is a more lucid version

543
00:22:36,650 --> 00:22:39,660
of those really bad, uh,
openings we saw.

544
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:40,650
-The credits, you know?
-Oh, the credits, yeah.

545
00:22:40,660 --> 00:22:43,160
Hey, that is if Cambot will man
the wall of keyboards.

546
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:44,660
-What do you say?
-Oh, good.

547
00:22:44,660 --> 00:22:46,660
Hey, and will you give us
that half-screen, uh,

548
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,670
posterization effect too,
Cambot?

549
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:49,660
-There we go.
-Uh, Joel...

550
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:50,660
--uh, what are we
supposed to do again?

551
00:22:50,670 --> 00:22:51,170
That's cool.

552
00:22:51,170 --> 00:22:52,670
Well, all you do is we play

553
00:22:52,670 --> 00:22:55,170
the characters
we talked about earlier

554
00:22:55,170 --> 00:22:56,170
and we run around and stuff.

555
00:22:56,170 --> 00:22:57,170
All right, got it.

556
00:22:57,170 --> 00:22:58,680
Frolic, cavort, parade,

557
00:22:58,670 --> 00:23:00,670
gad about the ship,
that sorta thing.

558
00:23:00,680 --> 00:23:02,180
-Uh, Joel?
-Yeah?

559
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,180
Isn't this kinda fruity?

560
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:05,180
Gee, I never really thought
about it that much.

561
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:07,180
-Joel, it is.
-Yep.

562
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:10,190
Well, no matter.
Anyway, uh, let's do it again.

563
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:13,680
-You ready, Cambot?
-Music. Here we go.

564
00:24:06,240 --> 00:24:09,250
[ Swords noise ]

565
00:24:14,250 --> 00:24:15,750
[ Swords noise ]

566
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:32,760
[ Swords noise ]

567
00:24:58,990 --> 00:25:01,490
[ Fighting grunts ]

568
00:25:01,500 --> 00:25:02,500
I thought that was pretty fun.

569
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,000
-Yeah.
-It was cool. [ Laughs ]

570
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:09,010
She's still looking
for the ends of the Earth here.

571
00:25:09,500 --> 00:25:11,000
Ends of the Earth,
ends of the Earth,

572
00:25:11,010 --> 00:25:12,510
I gotta get to the ends
of the Earth.

573
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:14,010
Ends of the Earth,
ends of the Earth.

574
00:25:14,010 --> 00:25:15,010
[ Pants ]

575
00:25:15,510 --> 00:25:17,510
- [ Screams ]
-Ooh, she's in love.

576
00:25:18,010 --> 00:25:20,020
So the ends of the Earth
are this way.

577
00:25:20,010 --> 00:25:21,010
Thank you.
[ Grunts ]

578
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:22,520
You idiot.

579
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:24,020
We don't even have
a doe license.

580
00:25:27,020 --> 00:25:28,530
That way.
Yeah.

581
00:25:28,520 --> 00:25:34,520
Ends of the Earth-- En--
Ends of the Earth-- [ Groans ]

582
00:25:35,530 --> 00:25:37,530
Let me see, uh, you were
playing a Titleist, right?

583
00:25:37,530 --> 00:25:38,540
Yep.

584
00:25:38,530 --> 00:25:40,030
You got a rotten lie,
let me tell ya.

585
00:25:43,540 --> 00:25:44,540
Daddy--

586
00:25:44,540 --> 00:25:47,540
Uh, uh, lady, can we have
our arrow back?

587
00:25:47,540 --> 00:25:50,050
Lady? Oh, Mrs. Lady!

588
00:25:50,540 --> 00:25:51,540
Oh-- [ Snorts ]

589
00:25:56,050 --> 00:25:57,050
Ah.

590
00:25:58,550 --> 00:26:00,050
Hey, why is she limping?

591
00:26:00,050 --> 00:26:02,050
'Cause she's got an arrow
in her chest.

592
00:26:02,060 --> 00:26:03,060
Oh, I can see-- Huh?

593
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:07,560
One thing still puzzles me,
Akronas.

594
00:26:07,560 --> 00:26:09,570
Use the handrails.
I invented them for a reason.

595
00:26:09,560 --> 00:26:11,060
Why east?

596
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:13,070
Why did your daughter
fly like an arrow

597
00:26:13,070 --> 00:26:14,570
straight towards the sun?

598
00:26:14,570 --> 00:26:16,070
Ooh, good metaphor.

599
00:26:16,570 --> 00:26:19,580
Of course, I could easily use
torture to make you tell me,

600
00:26:19,570 --> 00:26:21,070
but that would too simple.

601
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:23,080
-And too much fun.
-Spoil our little game.

602
00:26:23,580 --> 00:26:25,080
Yes.

603
00:26:25,580 --> 00:26:27,080
I see.

604
00:26:27,580 --> 00:26:30,590
It's quite obvious
that you're testing me.

605
00:26:30,580 --> 00:26:34,580
You want to verify
my powers of deduction.

606
00:26:34,590 --> 00:26:36,090
-Mm-hm.
-Very well.

607
00:26:37,090 --> 00:26:39,100
-Nice.
-Bring me the map.

608
00:26:39,090 --> 00:26:41,590
And bring me the head
of Gallagher.

609
00:26:42,100 --> 00:26:46,100
[ Bird sounds ]

610
00:26:46,600 --> 00:26:49,610
[ Horse whinny ]

611
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:50,600
[ Engine noise ]

612
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:52,100
Shh.

613
00:26:52,610 --> 00:26:55,610
- [ Wind noise ]
-Welcome to Death Valley Days.

614
00:26:55,610 --> 00:26:58,110
The driver's either missing
or he's dead.

615
00:26:58,110 --> 00:26:59,120
[ Chuckles ]

616
00:27:00,610 --> 00:27:01,610
Say...

617
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:06,120
Made this in shop class.
It's a letter opener.

618
00:27:06,620 --> 00:27:08,120
It's not perfect yet.

619
00:27:15,630 --> 00:27:17,630
A Mark Seven Production.

620
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:23,140
[ Hums ]

621
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:25,640
He doesn't give a tinker's damn
about anything.

622
00:27:25,640 --> 00:27:26,640
Nope.

623
00:27:28,140 --> 00:27:29,650
[ Owl noise ]

624
00:27:30,140 --> 00:27:32,640
Hey, did you just turn into
an owl and then back real fast?

625
00:27:32,650 --> 00:27:35,150
-Maybe it was too hot.
-Mm.

626
00:27:35,150 --> 00:27:37,650
-Mm-hm.
-It should be enough for now.

627
00:27:38,650 --> 00:27:41,150
-Gotta wait until it's cold.
-That could take forever.

628
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:42,660
Oh, help!

629
00:27:42,660 --> 00:27:43,660
-Huh?
-Hm?

630
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:45,660
Run! Look out, it's wet there!
I just mopped.

631
00:27:46,160 --> 00:27:47,660
Ator, help me, please.

632
00:27:49,660 --> 00:27:52,160
-Prepare everything for her.
-With pleasure, my liege.

633
00:27:53,670 --> 00:27:55,170
-Hey, he's washing with lava.
-The soap?

634
00:27:55,170 --> 00:27:57,170
Oh, no, the real thing.

635
00:27:57,170 --> 00:27:59,180
-Hm.
- [ Chuckles ]

636
00:27:59,670 --> 00:28:01,670
-It's Marmaduke.
- [ Dog panting ]

637
00:28:03,180 --> 00:28:05,180
[ Dog panting ]

638
00:28:05,180 --> 00:28:07,180
All right, good.
Okay, let's see.

639
00:28:07,180 --> 00:28:09,690
We've got the cow skin,
the banana leaves and the dog.

640
00:28:09,680 --> 00:28:11,680
That should be about everything.

641
00:28:12,190 --> 00:28:13,190
All we can do is pray,

642
00:28:13,690 --> 00:28:16,690
although we haven't thought
of any gods yet.

643
00:28:17,690 --> 00:28:19,700
Well, it's up to the dog.
No, Marmaduke!

644
00:28:19,690 --> 00:28:22,190
Don't use the triple over
end stitch! Bad dog!

645
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:24,200
[ Whines ]

646
00:28:24,700 --> 00:28:25,700
I could be wrong,

647
00:28:25,700 --> 00:28:28,710
but this arrow might have
something to do with her pain.

648
00:28:28,700 --> 00:28:29,700
Ah.

649
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:32,210
[ Licks, whines ]

650
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:33,710
-What do we got?
-She's okay.

651
00:28:33,710 --> 00:28:34,710
Yeah.

652
00:28:38,710 --> 00:28:39,710
Boy!

653
00:28:40,710 --> 00:28:42,210
Look at how primitive
their wet naps

654
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:43,720
were during the dark ages.

655
00:28:43,720 --> 00:28:44,720
Mm.

656
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:48,220
Yeah, it's a pretty big hole.

657
00:28:48,220 --> 00:28:50,230
I might need
another one of those.

658
00:28:58,230 --> 00:28:59,740
[ Chuckles ]

659
00:28:59,730 --> 00:29:01,230
Got the crazy idea, boss.

660
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,240
Let's make a giant cigar
out of her.

661
00:29:04,740 --> 00:29:06,740
What?
Would you quit your--?

662
00:29:06,740 --> 00:29:09,250
The entire area is deserted,
barren.

663
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:12,240
It's the best show tune ever!

664
00:29:12,250 --> 00:29:14,750
It's brassy, sassy,
it's a musical humdinger!

665
00:29:16,750 --> 00:29:19,760
Let's see...
[ Speaks in Latin ]

666
00:29:20,250 --> 00:29:21,250
Wait a minute.

667
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:23,760
-Ator!
-This is the magna carta!

668
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:29,770
So now we have it.

669
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:35,770
He was another pupil of yours,
wasn't he?

670
00:29:36,770 --> 00:29:39,280
Hm, kind of impressed
about his part in this film,

671
00:29:39,270 --> 00:29:40,770
isn't he?

672
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:45,780
Many stories have grown up
around this pupil of yours.

673
00:29:45,780 --> 00:29:47,280
I wish you'd grow up.

674
00:29:47,280 --> 00:29:48,790
But now the time has come...

675
00:29:50,280 --> 00:29:52,780
-...for me to discover...
-The manchild within.

676
00:29:52,790 --> 00:29:55,790
...proof of these stories.

677
00:29:57,790 --> 00:29:59,300
I pledge allegiance--

678
00:29:59,290 --> 00:30:00,790
This is really amazing.

679
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:02,300
Hm.

680
00:30:02,300 --> 00:30:03,800
Why, your knowledge of surgery

681
00:30:03,800 --> 00:30:05,300
surpasses even that
of The Great One.

682
00:30:05,300 --> 00:30:06,800
Who, Jackie Gleason?

683
00:30:07,800 --> 00:30:10,310
Oh, I'm just tallying up
your bill here.

684
00:30:10,300 --> 00:30:11,800
I'm ready to go now.

685
00:30:13,810 --> 00:30:15,310
No, you're not going.

686
00:30:16,810 --> 00:30:19,820
-I'll decide when you're ready.
-Little missy.

687
00:30:19,810 --> 00:30:22,810
-Journey is long.
- [ Hums ]

688
00:30:23,820 --> 00:30:25,820
Once we start,
there'll be no stopping.

689
00:30:26,320 --> 00:30:27,820
But I explained to you

690
00:30:27,820 --> 00:30:29,830
that my father
is in great danger.

691
00:30:29,820 --> 00:30:32,320
Danger--
How many A's in "danger"?

692
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:34,830
I understand the dangers
that face all men.

693
00:30:34,830 --> 00:30:35,830
All...

694
00:30:35,830 --> 00:30:37,330
...men.

695
00:30:38,330 --> 00:30:40,840
The wise one is very strong.

696
00:30:40,830 --> 00:30:42,830
-..ry strong.
-And will resist.

697
00:30:43,340 --> 00:30:44,840
But his heart is weak.

698
00:30:44,840 --> 00:30:47,340
-Heart is weak.
-That's the reason he sent me.

699
00:30:47,340 --> 00:30:48,850
-Sent me.
-What do you think he's writing?

700
00:30:49,340 --> 00:30:49,840
-The script?
-Yeah.

701
00:30:49,840 --> 00:30:51,340
Huh.

702
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:52,850
All right.

703
00:30:52,850 --> 00:30:54,850
But you must know this--

704
00:30:54,850 --> 00:30:56,850
Two plus two is fi--
I mean, four.

705
00:30:56,850 --> 00:30:58,350
If you're too weak...

706
00:30:58,850 --> 00:31:00,850
we'll have to leave you behind.

707
00:31:01,360 --> 00:31:02,860
Oh, thanks for the beer,
Gomez.

708
00:31:03,360 --> 00:31:05,360
But first you
must prove to us...

709
00:31:05,860 --> 00:31:09,870
if you are the daughter
of The Great One.

710
00:31:09,860 --> 00:31:12,860
If you can look bored
and speak haltingly, you're in.

711
00:31:16,370 --> 00:31:17,870
Come with me.

712
00:31:19,370 --> 00:31:20,870
No, not you, her.

713
00:31:21,380 --> 00:31:22,880
There she is.

714
00:31:28,380 --> 00:31:30,890
Too bad Gomez
didn't get a speaking role here.

715
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:32,890
Poor guy.

716
00:31:32,890 --> 00:31:34,390
Go in there.

717
00:31:35,390 --> 00:31:39,900
Oh, right, I'm a freshman
at a small Midwestern college.

718
00:31:39,890 --> 00:31:42,890
The small one
was dark with long hair.

719
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:47,900
Mila.

720
00:31:47,900 --> 00:31:49,910
Now sing something
from Paint Your Wagon.

721
00:31:49,900 --> 00:31:51,900
If you're really
the daughter of Akronas...

722
00:31:51,910 --> 00:31:54,410
Kronos Quartet? Oh.

723
00:31:55,910 --> 00:31:57,910
...then, you will know
what to do.

724
00:31:58,410 --> 00:31:59,420
Okay.

725
00:31:59,910 --> 00:32:02,910
Next on Current Affair:
"Women Behind Bars"!

726
00:32:03,420 --> 00:32:05,920
[ Hums Current Affairs theme ]

727
00:32:08,420 --> 00:32:09,430
Hm, okay.

728
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:11,420
Let's see now,
there's a Superball

729
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:12,930
and half a peanut

730
00:32:12,930 --> 00:32:15,430
and a length of kite string
and a carpenter's saw.

731
00:32:15,430 --> 00:32:17,430
What would McGyver do?

732
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:22,440
Is this right?

733
00:32:23,940 --> 00:32:26,440
-Hm. Mm-mm.
-No, wrong, cold.

734
00:32:26,440 --> 00:32:27,440
Very cold.

735
00:32:27,440 --> 00:32:28,950
-Freezing.
-Frigid.

736
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:31,440
-Freezing. Alaska.
-Mhm.

737
00:32:32,950 --> 00:32:33,950
Oh, you're a cute one,
aren't ya?

738
00:32:33,950 --> 00:32:34,950
[ Chuckles ]

739
00:32:35,450 --> 00:32:36,450
Getting warmer.

740
00:32:36,450 --> 00:32:39,460
-Hm, warm as toast.
-She made, uh--

741
00:32:39,450 --> 00:32:40,450
Very warm.

742
00:32:40,450 --> 00:32:42,950
She's making flash powder
from her own filth.

743
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:43,960
-Oh, neat.
- [ Vomiting noise ]

744
00:32:44,460 --> 00:32:45,460
Yee.

745
00:32:49,460 --> 00:32:51,960
-Uh-huh.
-Dibs.

746
00:32:52,470 --> 00:32:53,470
Rats.

747
00:32:57,970 --> 00:32:58,980
Uh-oh.

748
00:32:59,970 --> 00:33:00,970
Oh.

749
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:04,980
[ Singing ] Love, love, love!
Tu, tu, tu

750
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:07,980
They do have a lot of product
to burn off.

751
00:33:07,980 --> 00:33:08,990
Mm-hm.

752
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:13,480
Hm. I suppose she could
have just tried the lock.

753
00:33:14,990 --> 00:33:16,490
All done?

754
00:33:19,490 --> 00:33:21,490
Uh, Gomez, don't pass
in front of the actors.

755
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Please.

756
00:33:23,500 --> 00:33:25,500
When I left
your father's castle,

757
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:29,010
he told me that if ever
the geometric nucleus

758
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,500
could endanger
the world's peace...

759
00:33:30,500 --> 00:33:32,000
Huh?

760
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:34,010
...a messenger
would come to me

761
00:33:34,010 --> 00:33:36,510
and prove his identity
beyond a doubt.

762
00:33:37,510 --> 00:33:40,020
You owe me 50 bucks
for the door.

763
00:33:41,520 --> 00:33:44,020
-Let us go.
-Ancient Chinese secret, huh?

764
00:33:51,830 --> 00:33:53,330
Let's say that thanks
to your teaching,

765
00:33:53,330 --> 00:33:56,330
Ator has mastered
the forces of nature.

