1018
00:44:31,460 --> 00:44:33,460
Um, well, anyway, you know,
they give cool names

1019
00:44:33,470 --> 00:44:35,970
to TV shows like that, too.
Like, uh, White Shadow--

1020
00:44:36,470 --> 00:44:38,470
--could've been called, uh,
Haloed Hoop Honky.

1021
00:44:38,470 --> 00:44:39,480
- [ Laughs ]
-Or, uh...

1022
00:44:39,470 --> 00:44:41,470
Jake and the Fatman, you
could've called that um, well--

1023
00:44:41,470 --> 00:44:43,470
--uh, Jake and the Fatman.

1024
00:44:43,480 --> 00:44:44,980
Yeah, pretty much.
Yeah, yeah.

1025
00:44:45,480 --> 00:44:47,480
You know what occurs to me?
That when local TV stations

1026
00:44:47,480 --> 00:44:49,990
talk about the grand marshals
for their holiday parades,

1027
00:44:50,480 --> 00:44:52,480
what they're really saying
is Gavin MacLeod.

1028
00:44:52,490 --> 00:44:53,990
-Exactly.
-Oh, I got one.

1029
00:44:53,990 --> 00:44:56,490
A pre-recorded segment
that's, uh-

1030
00:44:56,990 --> 00:44:58,990
that goes into a program
is called a bumper.

1031
00:44:58,990 --> 00:45:00,500
-Oh, yeah?
-And actually it's really just--

1032
00:45:00,490 --> 00:45:01,490
- [ Buzzer sounds ]
-The movie's s--

1033
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:02,990
[ Scream and yell ]

1034
00:45:13,370 --> 00:45:15,870
-Oh, wow.
- [ Chuckles ]

1035
00:45:15,880 --> 00:45:17,380
[ Clears throat ]
Oh, boy.

1036
00:45:18,880 --> 00:45:21,880
Well, let's see, uh, "He who
reads these words of wit

1037
00:45:21,880 --> 00:45:22,890
eats these little balls--"

1038
00:45:22,880 --> 00:45:25,880
Oh, now that's immature,
even for The Dark Ages.

1039
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:28,890
Hm, "For a good time,
call Dong."

1040
00:45:28,890 --> 00:45:30,890
-Thong.
-Thong.

1041
00:45:32,890 --> 00:45:34,390
Here's-- Huh?

1042
00:45:34,390 --> 00:45:36,390
- [ Fighting noises ]
- [ Chuckles ]

1043
00:45:37,400 --> 00:45:39,400
They're kinda dumb,
they're easy to kill:

1044
00:45:39,400 --> 00:45:40,900
the American Gladiators.

1045
00:45:44,900 --> 00:45:45,900
Hm.

1046
00:45:47,910 --> 00:45:48,410
Ah.

1047
00:45:48,910 --> 00:45:50,410
-Hm.
-Something dull.

1048
00:45:50,910 --> 00:45:52,410
Come towards it, our friend.

1049
00:45:52,410 --> 00:45:57,420
By the stubbing of my thumb,
something stupid this way comes.

1050
00:45:58,420 --> 00:45:59,920
Aha, just as I thought.

1051
00:45:59,920 --> 00:46:01,920
-Hm.
-Checks out.

1052
00:46:01,920 --> 00:46:03,430
Meter man.

1053
00:46:05,430 --> 00:46:06,930
Knock it off up there.

1054
00:46:09,430 --> 00:46:11,930
Huh? "For a good time, call--"

1055
00:46:11,930 --> 00:46:12,940
Oh.

1056
00:46:12,930 --> 00:46:14,930
Stupid rock.
Stupid, stupid rock.

1057
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:17,940
Get-- Oh. Oh, man.

1058
00:46:18,440 --> 00:46:19,440
Did you find a way out?

1059
00:46:19,440 --> 00:46:20,940
Stupid rock.

1060
00:46:20,940 --> 00:46:22,440
Good thing you were here,
Gomez.

1061
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:24,450
We woulda never found it
without you.

1062
00:46:27,950 --> 00:46:28,950
Huh?

1063
00:46:29,950 --> 00:46:31,450
"Drizzle drazzle drozzle drone,
time for zis one to come home."

1064
00:46:31,450 --> 00:46:33,460
So Bob Hope owns all of that?

1065
00:46:33,450 --> 00:46:36,450
Yeah, yeah. We're thinkin'
of turning it into a 9-holer.

1066
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:37,460
-Hm.
-Yeah.

1067
00:46:38,460 --> 00:46:40,960
-You have failed, Sandur.
-Bad country singer.

1068
00:46:40,960 --> 00:46:43,470
-Bad Willie.
-You made me lose precious time!

1069
00:46:43,460 --> 00:46:45,960
If you had all the magical
powers you told me you had--

1070
00:46:45,970 --> 00:46:47,470
Again with the finger.

1071
00:46:48,470 --> 00:46:50,470
I don't see how I failed.

1072
00:46:50,470 --> 00:46:51,970
You don't, eh?

1073
00:46:52,470 --> 00:46:53,980
Well, you soon will.

1074
00:46:54,470 --> 00:46:55,470
Guards!

1075
00:46:56,480 --> 00:46:57,480
Hey, Paul Wellstone.

1076
00:46:57,980 --> 00:47:00,480
You'd think after all this time,

1077
00:47:00,480 --> 00:47:03,490
Sandur has been worthy
of your esteem.

1078
00:47:03,980 --> 00:47:07,980
And you are as guilty
of having failed as he is.

1079
00:47:08,990 --> 00:47:11,990
-Flog him!
-Thank you, sir.

1080
00:47:11,990 --> 00:47:15,000
-Please have mercy.
-I fear for you, Sandur.

1081
00:47:16,500 --> 00:47:19,000
Mercy does not dwell
in the hearts of those

1082
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:21,500
without spiritual strength
and wisdom.

1083
00:47:21,500 --> 00:47:23,510
Oh, bite me. It's fun.

1084
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:26,500
Very well.

1085
00:47:27,010 --> 00:47:28,010
Imprison him.

1086
00:47:28,010 --> 00:47:31,010
I'll employ some tricks
of my own against Ator

1087
00:47:31,010 --> 00:47:33,520
and you can use your time
to come up with something new

1088
00:47:33,510 --> 00:47:37,510
and it better be good, Sandur,
if you want to regain my esteem.

1089
00:47:37,520 --> 00:47:43,030
And I think you know how
important for you is my esteem.

1090
00:47:43,020 --> 00:47:44,020
Hm.

1091
00:47:44,020 --> 00:47:45,020
Okay. Okay,
I'll do linking rings.

1092
00:47:45,530 --> 00:47:46,530
I'll do bottom of the cup.

1093
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:48,030
I'll do metamorphosis.
Wait! Wait!

1094
00:47:53,030 --> 00:47:55,530
It's here.
Oh, we're already there.

1095
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,540
It's much too quiet here.

1096
00:47:57,540 --> 00:47:59,040
-Too, too quiet.
-Not a good sign.

1097
00:47:59,040 --> 00:48:00,540
[ Bird calls ]

1098
00:48:00,540 --> 00:48:02,540
I sense the presence
of something evil.

1099
00:48:02,540 --> 00:48:05,550
-That's you.
-Zor must be at work here.

1100
00:48:06,550 --> 00:48:08,050
Since we left the caves,

1101
00:48:08,550 --> 00:48:10,050
I've had the feeling
that we're being followed.

1102
00:48:10,550 --> 00:48:12,550
Ah, that's me, boss.
I'm right behind you.

1103
00:48:15,560 --> 00:48:17,560
I don't know,
but we'll soon find out.

1104
00:48:19,560 --> 00:48:21,060
[ Chuckles ]

1105
00:48:22,560 --> 00:48:23,570
-Huh?
-Look, there they are!

1106
00:48:24,060 --> 00:48:25,560
-What's this?
-Come on, quick! Hide!

1107
00:48:25,570 --> 00:48:29,070
Oh, no, they've jumped right
into a Kurosawa film.

1108
00:48:32,570 --> 00:48:34,580
-So it'll start making sense?
-Mm-hm.

1109
00:48:36,580 --> 00:48:38,080
Yep.

1110
00:48:39,080 --> 00:48:41,580
-Toshiro Mifune right there.
-Goody.

1111
00:48:41,580 --> 00:48:42,580
I'm huge.

1112
00:48:43,080 --> 00:48:44,080
-Hm.
-Dig me.

1113
00:48:44,580 --> 00:48:45,580
Yeah?

1114
00:48:47,090 --> 00:48:49,590
-Oh, no, a mime.
-Oh.

1115
00:48:50,090 --> 00:48:51,090
[ Chuckles ]

1116
00:48:54,590 --> 00:48:56,590
-Did he mention he's huge?
-Yeah.

1117
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:58,100
He does that.

1118
00:49:00,100 --> 00:49:03,610
Warriors, come out and play-ay.

1119
00:49:04,600 --> 00:49:05,600
[ Fighting noises ]

1120
00:49:06,610 --> 00:49:08,110
Now, you see,
I use two blades.

1121
00:49:08,110 --> 00:49:10,110
The first blade
lifts the head away

1122
00:49:10,110 --> 00:49:12,110
from the body before the head,

1123
00:49:12,110 --> 00:49:14,120
uh, can snap back
and then the, uh--

1124
00:49:14,110 --> 00:49:15,110
Yeah.

1125
00:49:15,110 --> 00:49:17,110
Yeah, below the skin level.
Yeah.

1126
00:49:17,620 --> 00:49:18,620
We get it.

1127
00:49:21,120 --> 00:49:23,630
Uh-huh.
Come on, come on.

1128
00:49:25,120 --> 00:49:27,120
Ooh, right in the breadbasket.

1129
00:49:31,630 --> 00:49:33,140
You know, the reason
this scene is so good

1130
00:49:33,130 --> 00:49:35,630
is because we care
about the characters.

1131
00:49:35,640 --> 00:49:37,640
-We do.
-Mm-hm.

1132
00:49:38,640 --> 00:49:41,140
-I mean, we do?
-Really do.

1133
00:49:44,640 --> 00:49:46,140
Hey, it's the life of the party.

1134
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:47,650
He's got a lampshade
on his head.

1135
00:49:48,150 --> 00:49:50,150
Gonna be the death
of the party soon.

1136
00:49:54,150 --> 00:49:54,650
Oh!

1137
00:49:55,660 --> 00:49:58,160
Oh. Wicker armor
courtesy Pier One.

1138
00:49:58,160 --> 00:49:59,660
Doesn't work too well.
It's just decorative.

1139
00:49:59,660 --> 00:50:00,660
Hurts, don't it?

1140
00:50:01,660 --> 00:50:03,170
Hai. Ho.

1141
00:50:04,160 --> 00:50:06,660
Look out,
it's Coco the Terrible.

1142
00:50:07,670 --> 00:50:10,670
- [ Laughs ] Goofy old mime.
- [ Chuckles ]

1143
00:50:12,170 --> 00:50:13,180
Hai.

1144
00:50:13,670 --> 00:50:14,670
Oops.

1145
00:50:14,670 --> 00:50:15,670
Ouch.

1146
00:50:17,680 --> 00:50:18,680
Ooh.

1147
00:50:19,180 --> 00:50:21,680
Okay, just like we rehearsed it.
Oh.

1148
00:50:22,180 --> 00:50:24,690
Over, across--
[ Chuckles ]

1149
00:50:24,680 --> 00:50:27,680
I will kill you!
[ Laughs ]

1150
00:50:28,690 --> 00:50:30,690
-Aw.
-Or not.

1151
00:50:30,690 --> 00:50:32,190
[ Attack yells ]

1152
00:50:32,190 --> 00:50:34,700
Hey, is this
where the kegger is?

1153
00:50:34,690 --> 00:50:36,690
We saw Mark's van in front.

1154
00:50:36,700 --> 00:50:37,700
No, way.

1155
00:50:37,700 --> 00:50:39,700
Uh, we just remembered, uh,

1156
00:50:39,700 --> 00:50:41,700
we didn't leave enough change
in the meter.

1157
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:42,700
We double-parked. Bye.

1158
00:50:42,700 --> 00:50:45,710
No use chasing.
Save your strength.

1159
00:50:45,710 --> 00:50:48,210
The castle of The Great One
is still far away.

1160
00:50:48,210 --> 00:50:49,710
To the end of the movie's
even further.

1161
00:50:49,710 --> 00:50:50,710
Well said.

1162
00:50:50,710 --> 00:50:52,210
-Yes.
-What I mean is...

1163
00:50:52,210 --> 00:50:53,720
Hey, matching vests.

1164
00:50:54,710 --> 00:50:56,210
--in stopping Ator--

1165
00:50:57,720 --> 00:50:59,720
ght, inadvertently, of course...

1166
00:51:00,220 --> 00:51:02,220
-Mm-hm.
-...also harm your daughter.

1167
00:51:02,220 --> 00:51:03,230
What do you say to that?

1168
00:51:03,220 --> 00:51:05,720
say you could drive a Mac truck
through your cues.

1169
00:51:05,730 --> 00:51:07,230
Tempo, tempo, pick it up!

1170
00:51:07,230 --> 00:51:11,730
I must admit, that as a murderer
you are most...

1171
00:51:12,730 --> 00:51:13,740
-...impressive.
-Mm-hm.

1172
00:51:13,730 --> 00:51:17,230
-But as an Andrew McCarthy fan--
-Whoo!

1173
00:51:18,740 --> 00:51:21,240
You will receive nothing
from me...

1174
00:51:21,240 --> 00:51:23,750
-...but pity.
-Aw.

1175
00:51:23,740 --> 00:51:26,740
-Careful, old man.
-Go to bed, old man.

1176
00:51:26,750 --> 00:51:29,250
-My patience has its limits.
-I'm aware of that.

1177
00:51:29,250 --> 00:51:30,750
As does your talents.

1178
00:51:30,750 --> 00:51:33,260
But I mustn't expect
too much from you.

1179
00:51:33,250 --> 00:51:33,750
[ Laughs ]

1180
00:51:33,750 --> 00:51:35,250
Patience, after all,

1181
00:51:35,250 --> 00:51:39,750
is a virtue which is found
only in the strong.

1182
00:51:40,260 --> 00:51:41,760
Hm.

1183
00:51:42,260 --> 00:51:43,770
-You're wonderful.
-Marry me.

1184
00:51:43,760 --> 00:51:45,760
You do amuse me.

1185
00:51:45,770 --> 00:51:47,770
-Hm.
-And provoke me.

1186
00:51:47,770 --> 00:51:48,770
-That is love, isn't it?
-Zor.

1187
00:51:48,770 --> 00:51:49,770
Hm.

1188
00:51:50,270 --> 00:51:51,270
What is it?

1189
00:51:51,270 --> 00:51:53,780
-Ator has escaped again.
-D'oh.

1190
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:57,780
Hi, Curt Gowdy here.

1191
00:51:57,780 --> 00:52:00,780
Join Thong and Phil Harris
and me out on the Idaho River,

1192
00:52:00,780 --> 00:52:02,280
fishing for trout.

1193
00:52:02,780 --> 00:52:05,790
Hey, hey, now try catching
a steak, Dong.

1194
00:52:06,290 --> 00:52:07,790
-Thong.
-Uh, Thong. [ Chuckles ]

1195
00:52:10,790 --> 00:52:14,300
Uh, Ator, what's your dream?

1196
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:20,800
How big is God?

1197
00:52:23,800 --> 00:52:25,300
For a moment back there,

1198
00:52:25,300 --> 00:52:27,800
I had the feeling you knew
those men that attacked us.

1199
00:52:27,810 --> 00:52:28,810
-Did you?
-Yes.

1200
00:52:28,810 --> 00:52:30,810
Well, we played
varsity together.

1201
00:52:31,310 --> 00:52:32,310
I do.

1202
00:52:32,310 --> 00:52:33,820
Who were they?

1203
00:52:34,310 --> 00:52:37,310
They're the survivors
of the noble tribe of Han.

1204
00:52:38,320 --> 00:52:40,320
They worship the God of War...

1205
00:52:40,820 --> 00:52:41,820
Soko.

1206
00:52:41,820 --> 00:52:44,830
Soko? I know that name.

1207
00:52:45,320 --> 00:52:48,820
-Oh, he dated my friend Sharon.
-Lord of the northern territory.

1208
00:52:49,830 --> 00:52:52,330
Uh, what's, uh,
Miles sitting on?

1209
00:52:52,830 --> 00:52:54,340
I don't wanna know.

1210
00:52:54,830 --> 00:52:56,830
In a great battle
against the Han,

1211
00:52:56,840 --> 00:52:57,840
Zor exterminated them.

1212
00:52:57,840 --> 00:53:00,340
But spared the lives
of three samurai

1213
00:53:00,340 --> 00:53:02,840
and then used them to kill
his own brother

1214
00:53:02,840 --> 00:53:03,850
and usurp power.

1215
00:53:03,840 --> 00:53:05,840
Oh, if this is
another flashback,

1216
00:53:05,850 --> 00:53:06,850
I gotta go get a sandwich.

1217
00:53:07,350 --> 00:53:09,850
-Do you think that Zor will--
-Oh, it's okay.

1218
00:53:10,350 --> 00:53:12,350
Do you think my father's
still alive?

1219
00:53:12,350 --> 00:53:13,360
Oh, sure. [ Laughs ]

1220
00:53:14,850 --> 00:53:17,850
Zor wants to possess
your father's knowledge, Mila.

1221
00:53:17,860 --> 00:53:20,360
-And your mother's wardrobe.
-Ooh.

1222
00:53:20,360 --> 00:53:22,860
-And the geometric nucleus.
-Hmm.

1223
00:53:24,860 --> 00:53:29,860
No... your father's safe
so long as he has it.

1224
00:53:31,870 --> 00:53:34,880
Uh, that's enough fish, Dong.
Thank you.

1225
00:53:34,870 --> 00:53:36,370
Thank you very much, Dong.
That's enough fish.

1226
00:53:36,380 --> 00:53:37,880
Just a few dozen more.

1227
00:53:38,880 --> 00:53:40,880
Why did you go
and live so far away?

1228
00:53:41,880 --> 00:53:42,880
Well, it's on the bus line.

1229
00:53:42,880 --> 00:53:45,890
Your father taught me the path
I must follow.

1230
00:53:45,890 --> 00:53:47,390
It is for this
I live the way I do.

1231
00:53:47,390 --> 00:53:48,890
Mm-hm.

1232
00:53:51,390 --> 00:53:53,900
But shouldn't a man's destiny...

1233
00:53:53,890 --> 00:53:55,890
Oh, I thought you were gonna
say something else.

1234
00:53:55,900 --> 00:53:57,900
...put aside the desires
of his heart?

1235
00:53:57,900 --> 00:53:59,900
Man's destiny is always
predetermined...

1236
00:53:59,900 --> 00:54:00,900
Oh, he's a Calvinist.

1237
00:54:00,900 --> 00:54:02,900
...by the true desires
of his heart.

1238
00:54:03,400 --> 00:54:06,400
I know what mine is, and I
must follow it alone, Mila.

1239
00:54:07,910 --> 00:54:10,910
I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to pry.

1240
00:54:11,410 --> 00:54:13,420
That's all right.
I'm glad you asked.

1241
00:54:14,410 --> 00:54:15,910
What's your major?

1242
00:54:16,920 --> 00:54:17,920
Thong?

1243
00:54:17,920 --> 00:54:19,420
-Mm-hm?
-The fish is ready.

1244
00:54:22,420 --> 00:54:23,430
Oh, wow.

1245
00:54:23,420 --> 00:54:24,920
What I wouldn't give
for a Weed Eater right now.

1246
00:54:27,930 --> 00:54:28,930
Hm?

1247
00:54:29,430 --> 00:54:31,430
[ Singing ]
La la la de dah

1248
00:54:31,930 --> 00:54:34,440
-Hm?
-No! Don't kill us.

1249
00:54:34,930 --> 00:54:36,930
Uh, what will you give me?

1250
00:54:37,440 --> 00:54:38,940
Okay, you talked me into it.

1251
00:54:38,940 --> 00:54:40,940
Huh, what?
Mom and Dad, Uncle Dave?

1252
00:54:40,940 --> 00:54:42,940
Oh.
[ Clears throat ]

1253
00:54:47,450 --> 00:54:48,450
-Mila.
-What is it?

1254
00:54:48,450 --> 00:54:50,450
Someone's coming. Look.

1255
00:54:50,450 --> 00:54:52,450
-Cover your hip.
-Get dressed.

1256
00:54:53,950 --> 00:54:56,950
-Who are you?
-Uh, we're pirates.

1257
00:54:56,960 --> 00:54:59,960
-What do you want?
-Look, you captured us.

1258
00:55:01,960 --> 00:55:03,470
[ Clears throat ]
Line.

1259
00:55:03,960 --> 00:55:07,460
-Where do you come from?
-Everywhere and nowhere.

1260
00:55:07,470 --> 00:55:08,470
Mm-hm.

1261
00:55:09,970 --> 00:55:12,970
-Somebody say something.
-Well, answer.

1262
00:55:13,970 --> 00:55:15,470
Can't you speak?

1263
00:55:15,980 --> 00:55:16,980
We're from Sulijen.

1264
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:18,980
[ Buzzer noise ] Wrong answer,
but thanks for playing.

1265
00:55:18,980 --> 00:55:20,480
Sulijen?

1266
00:55:21,980 --> 00:55:23,490
Yes. It's to the north,
not far from here.

1267
00:55:23,980 --> 00:55:26,480
-Yeah, I worked out there.
-I know.

1268
00:55:27,490 --> 00:55:28,990
It's where my parents
were born.

1269
00:55:29,490 --> 00:55:31,990
Then you're... Ator.

1270
00:55:32,490 --> 00:55:33,500
You're called The Great Master.

1271
00:55:33,490 --> 00:55:34,990
Yep. Yeah,
that's me pretty much.

1272
00:55:35,490 --> 00:55:36,490
Speak not in fear with me.

1273
00:55:37,500 --> 00:55:41,000
Much evil has fallen
on the people of our village.

1274
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:43,000
In order to survive,
we must make an offering

1275
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:44,510
to the god of the Kung.

1276
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:48,000
Human sacrifice to the serpent
god on every full moon.

1277
00:55:48,510 --> 00:55:50,510
Besides, our people
are not warriors.

1278
00:55:51,010 --> 00:55:52,510
We're only poor farmers.

1279
00:55:52,510 --> 00:55:55,520
If we don't get help soon,
we'll all die.

1280
00:55:55,510 --> 00:55:58,010
Hm, I like it.
Make it shorter, I'll buy it.

1281
00:55:58,020 --> 00:56:01,020
The Kungs have always
demanded the blood of Man.

1282
00:56:01,020 --> 00:56:06,530
-Yeah, they're funny that way.
-We must act quickly.

1283
00:56:07,530 --> 00:56:10,530
But not right now.
In a minute or two.

1284
00:56:10,530 --> 00:56:11,530
Half an hour maybe.

1285
00:56:11,530 --> 00:56:13,540
Wow, check out the way
that guy moves, huh?

1286
00:56:13,530 --> 00:56:16,030
What do you intend to do, Ator?

1287
00:56:16,540 --> 00:56:18,040
We'll take them back
to the village,

1288
00:56:18,040 --> 00:56:19,540
and I'll speak
with their people.

1289
00:56:19,540 --> 00:56:22,040
-The Village People?
-Mm-hm.

1290
00:56:22,540 --> 00:56:24,050
The Kungs will kill us!

1291
00:56:25,540 --> 00:56:27,040
I... think...

1292
00:56:27,050 --> 00:56:28,550
-We should run!
-Run!

1293
00:56:28,550 --> 00:56:31,550
-Ah!
-No. Let them go, Thong.

1294
00:56:31,550 --> 00:56:33,050
If you love something,
let it go.

1295
00:56:33,050 --> 00:56:34,060
Fear has blinded them.

1296
00:56:34,050 --> 00:56:35,550
We'll go without them.

1297
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:37,560
We'll hurry down there.

1298
00:56:38,060 --> 00:56:39,560
Who will be the first
to volunteer?

1299
00:56:43,560 --> 00:56:46,560
I'll be doing the death scene
from Camille, thank you.

1300
00:56:46,570 --> 00:56:48,070
Hm.

1301
00:56:49,570 --> 00:56:51,070
And the next?

1302
00:56:51,070 --> 00:56:54,080
Come forward,
Cowardly Lion.

1303
00:56:55,070 --> 00:56:56,570
Oh, it's a woman.

1304
00:56:57,580 --> 00:56:59,080
Mm-hm.

1305
00:57:00,080 --> 00:57:01,080
Hm.

1306
00:57:01,080 --> 00:57:04,590
-I could use a man like you.
-And I do mean use.

1307
00:57:07,590 --> 00:57:11,090
-Uh, you, uh, never mind.
- [ Chuckles ]

1308
00:57:11,090 --> 00:57:13,090
-Nice try.
-Yeah.

1309
00:57:16,100 --> 00:57:18,600
-We need another.
-I'll go.

1310
00:57:19,600 --> 00:57:21,100
Uh, no, you went last time.
One to a customer.

1311
00:57:21,100 --> 00:57:22,600
Oh, no, not you, my dear.

1312
00:57:22,600 --> 00:57:25,110
Our family's already given
one life to the Kung.

1313
00:57:25,600 --> 00:57:28,600
Grandmother, else another
will have to take my place.

1314
00:57:29,610 --> 00:57:32,110
-Nancy Walker in a cameo role.
-Hm.

1315
00:57:33,110 --> 00:57:34,620
-Wait!
-Hey!

1316
00:57:34,610 --> 00:57:38,610
It's Speedy Delivery Guy,
and has he got a package.

1317
00:57:40,120 --> 00:57:42,120
-Stop!
-In the name of love.

1318
00:57:45,620 --> 00:57:47,120
Just wait for me.
I'll be down in a minute.

1319
00:57:47,130 --> 00:57:49,130
Just stand there.
I'm coming.

1320
00:57:49,630 --> 00:57:51,130
-[ Sighs ]
-Okay. Well, now.

1321
00:57:51,630 --> 00:57:53,640
Oh, I thought this was
the Anderson party.

1322
00:57:53,630 --> 00:57:56,630
Sorry. [ Chuckles ]
I'll just be on my way.

1323
00:57:58,140 --> 00:57:59,640
Who is this gentle stranger

1324
00:57:59,640 --> 00:58:02,140
with pecs like melons
and knees of fringe?

1325
00:58:03,140 --> 00:58:04,650
Ator.

1326
00:58:04,640 --> 00:58:05,640
Where?

1327
00:58:05,640 --> 00:58:06,640
You have chosen a day
of mourning

1328
00:58:06,650 --> 00:58:08,650
to visit the village
of your parents.

1329
00:58:08,650 --> 00:58:09,650
Afternoon? Really?

1330
00:58:09,650 --> 00:58:11,150
I've come to help you fight.

1331
00:58:12,650 --> 00:58:14,160
We're not fighting men.

1332
00:58:14,150 --> 00:58:16,150
-The Kungs are--
-You must.

1333
00:58:17,160 --> 00:58:19,660
If you go on like this,
none of you will be left alive.

1334
00:58:19,660 --> 00:58:21,660
[ Goofy chuckles ]
Dude looks like a lady.

1335
00:58:21,660 --> 00:58:23,160
[ Goofy chuckles ]

1336
00:58:26,670 --> 00:58:27,670
Where's Ravani?

1337
00:58:27,670 --> 00:58:29,670
-Who?
-Ravani has left us.

1338
00:58:29,670 --> 00:58:30,670
'Cause he had nothing to do
with the film.

1339
00:58:30,670 --> 00:58:32,670
He was too old to guide us.

1340
00:58:33,170 --> 00:58:35,180
I have taken his place
as the elder.

1341
00:58:35,670 --> 00:58:37,670
He was a proud,
courageous man.

1342
00:58:37,680 --> 00:58:39,680
But dumber
than a bag of hammers.

1343
00:58:41,680 --> 00:58:45,190
He never would have allowed
such submissive behavior.

1344
00:58:45,180 --> 00:58:47,180
-What, did you call me a wussie?
-Mm-hm.

1345
00:58:47,190 --> 00:58:48,690
You must not lose heart.

1346
00:58:48,690 --> 00:58:50,690
-I see great courage here.
-Because a guy will eat it.

1347
00:58:50,690 --> 00:58:53,700
Most of your young people
willingly sacrifice themselves

1348
00:58:53,690 --> 00:58:55,190
-to be victims of the Kungs...
-Coffee?

1349
00:58:55,190 --> 00:58:56,690
-...and their serpent god.
-Tea?

1350
00:58:56,700 --> 00:58:58,200
-Nuts.
-Put that courage to better use

1351
00:58:58,200 --> 00:58:59,200
and fight back,

1352
00:58:59,200 --> 00:59:01,700
for the Kungs can be defeated,
and I will help you.

1353
00:59:01,700 --> 00:59:04,710
You will regain your freedom
and live in peace again.

1354
00:59:04,700 --> 00:59:07,700
Surprise is an excellent weapon.
-Hi, Estelle.

1355
00:59:08,710 --> 00:59:09,710
How you doing, Mickey?

1356
00:59:09,710 --> 00:59:11,710
One of intelligence
rather than brute strength.

1357
00:59:11,710 --> 00:59:13,210
Posture, people.

1358
00:59:13,710 --> 00:59:16,210
-Let's snap it up a bit.
-But they are stupid as well.

1359
00:59:16,220 --> 00:59:17,220
It's Gary.

1360
00:59:17,220 --> 00:59:19,220
They always make frontal attacks
against their enemies.

1361
00:59:19,220 --> 00:59:20,720
They know you have been pacified

1362
00:59:20,720 --> 00:59:23,220
and won't be expecting
any resistance from you.

1363
00:59:23,220 --> 00:59:23,730
Uh-huh.

1364
00:59:24,220 --> 00:59:25,220
What we must do is prepare

1365
00:59:25,220 --> 00:59:27,220
a trap for them
when they arrive.

1366
00:59:27,230 --> 00:59:28,230
Right here.

1367
00:59:28,730 --> 00:59:30,230
And then we'll take them
by surprise.

1368
00:59:31,730 --> 00:59:33,740
-Mm-hm.
-The village is well-situated.

1369
00:59:33,730 --> 00:59:34,730
And so am I.

1370
00:59:35,730 --> 00:59:37,730
Those rocks will act as a wall
to protect you.

1371
00:59:37,740 --> 00:59:39,240
And vice versa.

1372
00:59:39,240 --> 00:59:40,740
That side is impassible
to horses,

1373
00:59:40,740 --> 00:59:42,740
so they'll have to attack
from over there.

1374
00:59:43,740 --> 00:59:45,240
To fortify that exposed side,

1375
00:59:45,240 --> 00:59:48,240
I'll need several sharp stakes,
ropes and three men to help me.

1376
00:59:49,250 --> 00:59:51,250
You and you two...

1377
00:59:52,750 --> 00:59:53,760
come with me.

1378
00:59:55,750 --> 00:59:58,250
-You afraid?
-N-- No. [ Nervous laugh ]

1379
00:59:58,260 --> 01:00:00,260
Won't you fight
to save your people?

1380
01:00:00,260 --> 01:00:01,260
No. I will.

1381
01:00:01,760 --> 01:00:03,770
-I wanna fight.
-For my right to party.

1382
01:00:04,760 --> 01:00:06,760
-Who else will join him?
-All done back there?

1383
01:00:06,770 --> 01:00:08,270
Aren't there any more
of you here

1384
01:00:08,270 --> 01:00:09,770
worthy of being called men?

1385
01:00:09,770 --> 01:00:12,770
Come on, we can win.
I'm sure of it. Step forward.

1386
01:00:12,770 --> 01:00:14,280
Or are you no better
than sheep...

1387
01:00:14,270 --> 01:00:15,770
...who are led to the slaughter?

1388
01:00:15,770 --> 01:00:16,770
Baa. [ Laugh ]

1389
01:00:16,780 --> 01:00:19,780
-...too harshly. We are people--
-We need more Calgon.

1390
01:00:20,780 --> 01:00:22,280
My husband's some hot shot.

1391
01:00:22,280 --> 01:00:24,790
Ancient Chinese secret, huh?

1392
01:00:27,290 --> 01:00:29,790
Ator's prehistoric cave dwellers
of Milwaukee

1393
01:00:29,790 --> 01:00:30,790
are a long way apart.

1394
01:00:30,790 --> 01:00:32,790
But they have
one thing in common.

1395
01:00:32,790 --> 01:00:35,800
Caveland means
the best human hearts available,

1396
01:00:35,790 --> 01:00:38,290
and Milwaukee means sacred wine.

1397
01:00:38,300 --> 01:00:39,800
Now, Ator...

1398
01:00:40,300 --> 01:00:41,300
Cream or sugar?

1399
01:00:42,300 --> 01:00:44,810
st, let us drink to your return.

1400
01:00:45,300 --> 01:00:47,800
-Okay, let's do that.
-Then we will discuss your plan.

1401
01:00:47,810 --> 01:00:49,810
Drink it all. Sometimes
the poison's on the bottom.

1402
01:00:49,810 --> 01:00:51,810
--the village of your ancestors.

1403
01:00:51,810 --> 01:00:53,820
-May your stay--
-I've heard this part.

1404
01:00:53,810 --> 01:00:54,810
-For all of us.
-Hi, Walt.

1405
01:00:54,810 --> 01:00:57,310
I thank you
and drink to the health,

1406
01:00:57,320 --> 01:00:58,820
prosperity and liberty
of your people.

1407
01:00:58,820 --> 01:00:59,820
Hey, not bad.

1408
01:01:01,320 --> 01:01:04,830
Hm.
Champagne makes me giggly.

1409
01:01:04,820 --> 01:01:05,820
[ Giggles ]

1410
01:01:06,330 --> 01:01:08,830
But let us organize ourselves.

1411
01:01:08,830 --> 01:01:10,830
I smell a rat, a big commie rat.

1412
01:01:10,830 --> 01:01:13,840
I'll need your strongest men
to build defenses.

1413
01:01:13,830 --> 01:01:15,330
It's Timothy Leary.

1414
01:01:15,330 --> 01:01:17,830
I guess Liddy will have to do
the tour without him.

1415
01:01:17,840 --> 01:01:19,340
Let's get to work.

1416
01:01:25,340 --> 01:01:26,840
My name is Ravani.

1417
01:01:26,850 --> 01:01:29,350
Tell Ator
they're going to trap him.

1418
01:01:29,350 --> 01:01:30,850
Mm-hm.

1419
01:01:30,850 --> 01:01:33,860
Yeah, yeah.
Get some sleep, Quentin, okay?

1420
01:01:33,850 --> 01:01:35,350
Is your ear drained?
Good.

1421
01:01:35,350 --> 01:01:36,350
Hello?

1422
01:01:36,860 --> 01:01:38,360
Your spit bucket's full.

1423
01:01:38,860 --> 01:01:41,860
Okay, so, uh,
I just go now, okay?

1424
01:01:41,860 --> 01:01:44,870
Um, I just leave the sign on
so the maid makes the room?

1425
01:01:45,360 --> 01:01:48,360
Okay.
[ Hums ]

1426
01:01:48,870 --> 01:01:49,870
I close the door.

1427
01:01:55,870 --> 01:02:00,370
Are you done with your drink?
[ Evil laugh ]

1428
01:02:01,380 --> 01:02:05,390
We secretly switched Ator's
coffee with Folgers crystals.

1429
01:02:05,380 --> 01:02:06,880
Let's watch.

1430
01:02:09,890 --> 01:02:10,890
Huh?

1431
01:02:11,890 --> 01:02:13,900
-He is huge.
-Timber!

1432
01:02:14,390 --> 01:02:18,890
All right. Now we call this film
The Wong Dwellers. Aw, yeah.

1433
01:02:18,900 --> 01:02:19,900
Thong.

1434
01:02:19,900 --> 01:02:21,900
Thong. Yeah, Thong.
Thorry.

1435
01:02:21,900 --> 01:02:24,910
Satellite picture shows clouds
are coming in from the west,

1436
01:02:24,900 --> 01:02:27,400
but this should burn off
by about noon.

1437
01:02:27,910 --> 01:02:30,910
Before the dawn of time,
a race of druids.

1438
01:02:30,910 --> 01:02:34,920
Nobody knew who they were
or where they came from.

1439
01:02:34,910 --> 01:02:35,910
Cool.

1440
01:02:35,910 --> 01:02:38,410
Boy, that cleared up
really quick.

1441
01:02:38,420 --> 01:02:39,920
I told you it would.

1442
01:02:42,420 --> 01:02:43,930
We've been betrayed.

1443
01:02:43,920 --> 01:02:45,920
-Oh, darn it.
-But still alive.

1444
01:02:46,930 --> 01:02:48,430
-Think so?
-Thong is free.

1445
01:02:48,930 --> 01:02:51,430
I wonder if it wouldn't have
been easier--

1446
01:02:51,430 --> 01:02:54,440
if we had just kept on going
to the aid of my father.

1447
01:02:54,430 --> 01:02:56,430
Oh. Monday morning quarterback.

1448
01:02:56,440 --> 01:02:58,940
No one's life is more important
than another's.

1449
01:02:58,940 --> 01:02:59,940
Except mine.

1450
01:03:00,440 --> 01:03:02,940
Your father would have
done the same.

1451
01:03:02,940 --> 01:03:04,450
Wear a tiny leather bikini?

1452
01:03:04,440 --> 01:03:05,440
Hmm?

1453
01:03:07,450 --> 01:03:10,450
This is CNN, Luke.

1454
01:03:12,450 --> 01:03:14,960
Check it out, they worship
the Munsingwear Penguin.

1455
01:03:17,460 --> 01:03:18,960
Uh, pardon us, did you see

1456
01:03:18,960 --> 01:03:20,960
a tiny little fox
run through here?

1457
01:03:21,960 --> 01:03:22,960
No?

1458
01:03:25,960 --> 01:03:27,460
The village elder was the one

1459
01:03:27,970 --> 01:03:29,470
who lured you
to come to help us.

1460
01:03:29,970 --> 01:03:32,970
In other words, those two
were part of the plan.

1461
01:03:32,970 --> 01:03:33,980
Yes.

1462
01:03:33,970 --> 01:03:34,970
I wish they were part
of the plot.

1463
01:03:34,970 --> 01:03:36,970
Some of us were against it
and wanted to fight,

1464
01:03:36,980 --> 01:03:38,980
but the majority
were too terrified.

1465
01:03:38,980 --> 01:03:41,480
The elder's going
to hand you over to the Kungs.

1466
01:03:41,480 --> 01:03:43,990
In exchange, they promise
to stop killing our people.

1467
01:03:43,980 --> 01:03:45,980
-All right, who's talking?
-I can't figure it out.

1468
01:03:45,980 --> 01:03:48,480
-Must be the director.
-...allied with Zor.

1469
01:03:49,490 --> 01:03:50,990
And what happened to Ravani?

1470
01:03:50,990 --> 01:03:53,490
The new elder has been
slowly poisoning him,

1471
01:03:53,490 --> 01:03:55,500
because he knew Ravani
would warn you if he could.

1472
01:03:55,490 --> 01:03:56,490
Fun.

1473
01:03:56,500 --> 01:03:58,000
I think Ravani must be dead
by now.

1474
01:03:58,500 --> 01:03:59,500
Yah! Yah!

1475
01:03:59,500 --> 01:04:01,500
Hey, it's Teddy Roosevelt
and the Roughriders.

1476
01:04:01,500 --> 01:04:03,000
I think it's the Kurds.

1477
01:04:03,000 --> 01:04:05,010
-And whey? [ Chuckles ]
-Yes, whey.

1478
01:04:05,000 --> 01:04:06,000
[ Laughs ]

1479
01:04:06,000 --> 01:04:08,000
They are terrifying, aren't
they? With those bandanas...

1480
01:04:08,510 --> 01:04:10,510
And they all look
very Machiavellian

1481
01:04:10,510 --> 01:04:12,010
with their shirts off.

1482
01:04:12,010 --> 01:04:13,510
-Yeah.
-Machiavellian?

1483
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:19,020
-Hiya, Phil.
-Morning, Tom.

1484
01:04:19,020 --> 01:04:20,520
A month has now passed,
old one.

1485
01:04:22,020 --> 01:04:25,530
-Have you done what you said?
-We have kept our promise.

1486
01:04:25,520 --> 01:04:27,520
Now you must keep yours.

1487
01:04:28,530 --> 01:04:31,030
I give you Ator, and in return,

1488
01:04:31,030 --> 01:04:33,530
our village will no longer
have to sacrifice

1489
01:04:33,530 --> 01:04:34,540
to your serpent god.

1490
01:04:35,030 --> 01:04:37,530
-Ah!
-Uh, that must mean "no".

1491
01:04:38,540 --> 01:04:40,540
-I think so.
-Oh!

1492
01:04:41,540 --> 01:04:42,540
Grr!

1493
01:04:45,540 --> 01:04:46,540
Yeehoo!

1494
01:04:48,050 --> 01:04:50,050
[ Screaming ]

1495
01:04:50,050 --> 01:04:51,550
These are the pillage people.
[ Chuckles ]

1496
01:04:51,550 --> 01:04:53,050
[ Screaming ]

1497
01:04:53,550 --> 01:04:54,560
-No!
-No!

1498
01:04:55,550 --> 01:04:59,550
It's not fair. I'm the star
of the show. [ Sobs ]

1499
01:05:09,870 --> 01:05:12,870
Oh, duh, I'm sure.
My hair is getting singed.

1500
01:05:12,870 --> 01:05:15,880
Last time I go club-hopping
with this guy.

1501
01:05:16,370 --> 01:05:18,370
Honey,
start lighting those huts.

1502
01:05:18,380 --> 01:05:19,880
The other two...

1503
01:05:20,380 --> 01:05:21,380
We'll get them later.

1504
01:05:21,380 --> 01:05:22,880
A job well done.

1505
01:05:24,380 --> 01:05:25,380
No!

1506
01:05:25,880 --> 01:05:26,880
No!

1507
01:05:27,390 --> 01:05:28,390
Please.

1508
01:05:28,890 --> 01:05:29,890
Oh.

1509
01:05:31,890 --> 01:05:34,400
Looks like the back lot
at Universal.

1510
01:05:34,390 --> 01:05:35,890
No, no, ah!

1511
01:05:35,890 --> 01:05:37,890
Feel the burn.
Come on, go for the burn.

1512
01:05:39,400 --> 01:05:40,900
Hey, here's just a wild idea:

1513
01:05:40,900 --> 01:05:42,900
why don't you rotate
