1699
01:13:37,880 --> 01:13:38,880
Now her.

1700
01:13:39,380 --> 01:13:40,380
Uh-oh.

1701
01:13:40,380 --> 01:13:42,880
Come on, in you go.
Get in the bidet, sister.

1702
01:13:42,880 --> 01:13:45,390
-[ Struggles ]
-Insy-winsy, come on.

1703
01:13:47,390 --> 01:13:48,890
-Aha!
-Ator, look out!

1704
01:13:51,390 --> 01:13:52,890
-Here we go.
-[ Groans ]

1705
01:13:53,390 --> 01:13:54,900
Now we finally have some action.

1706
01:13:55,390 --> 01:13:56,890
-Oop.
-All right.

1707
01:13:57,400 --> 01:13:59,900
-Ator, be careful!
-Let's get busy.

1708
01:14:01,400 --> 01:14:03,900
Oh, no, we gotta go now.

1709
01:14:03,900 --> 01:14:04,910
-Oh, no.
-Just when it's getting good.

1710
01:14:05,400 --> 01:14:06,900
-Yeah.
-Dag gone it.

1711
01:14:06,900 --> 01:14:08,400
-That's just the way it is.
-Carry me.

1712
01:14:08,410 --> 01:14:09,910
-No.
-Forget it.

1713
01:14:12,910 --> 01:14:14,410
I'll kill you myself, Ator!

1714
01:14:22,920 --> 01:14:23,920
[ Hums ]

1715
01:14:23,920 --> 01:14:25,930
-Oh, say, Joel?
-Mm-hm?

1716
01:14:25,920 --> 01:14:27,920
Why is it when they punch
each other in this movie

1717
01:14:27,930 --> 01:14:29,430
it doesn't sound anything
like a punch?

1718
01:14:29,430 --> 01:14:30,930
Yeah, it sounds more
like a bag full of sardines

1719
01:14:31,430 --> 01:14:32,930
thrown against a pole barn.

1720
01:14:32,930 --> 01:14:34,940
Well, you're not too far off,
you skipsters.

1721
01:14:34,930 --> 01:14:37,430
You see, sound effects artists
use a technique

1722
01:14:37,440 --> 01:14:38,940
called foley to create
those sounds.

1723
01:14:38,940 --> 01:14:39,940
It's interesting, isn't it?

1724
01:14:39,940 --> 01:14:40,940
-Mm, no.
-Not really.

1725
01:14:40,940 --> 01:14:41,940
I don't think so. No.

1726
01:14:41,940 --> 01:14:43,440
I think maybe
you should humor me.

1727
01:14:43,440 --> 01:14:44,950
-Oh, okay.
-Sure.

1728
01:14:44,940 --> 01:14:46,440
-Oh, foley, what do you know?
-Very interesting.

1729
01:14:46,440 --> 01:14:47,440
-Sounds cool.
-Yeah, tell us.

1730
01:14:47,450 --> 01:14:48,950
Well, I'm glad you asked, boys.

1731
01:14:48,950 --> 01:14:50,950
Foley artists
use a lot of ordinary items

1732
01:14:50,950 --> 01:14:52,950
found around the home
or office

1733
01:14:52,950 --> 01:14:54,960
to create convincing
sound effects.

1734
01:14:54,950 --> 01:14:57,950
Oh, like the sound of, uh,
fists slamming into jaws?

1735
01:14:57,960 --> 01:15:00,460
Right. But let's get started
with something simple.

1736
01:15:00,460 --> 01:15:02,460
An easy way to make
a horse trotting

1737
01:15:02,460 --> 01:15:03,960
is to use a pair of coconuts.

1738
01:15:03,960 --> 01:15:05,470
-Oh.
-Cocy-nuts?

1739
01:15:05,460 --> 01:15:05,960
Right.
Now listen.

1740
01:15:06,460 --> 01:15:07,460
- [ Clops ]
-Ah.

1741
01:15:07,470 --> 01:15:08,970
It's the sound
of a quarter horse

1742
01:15:08,970 --> 01:15:10,970
gelding on
a cobblestone courtyard.

1743
01:15:10,970 --> 01:15:11,970
It's pretty convincing,
isn't it?

1744
01:15:12,470 --> 01:15:14,980
Yeah, but what if the horse
is on grass, hm?

1745
01:15:14,970 --> 01:15:17,470
Oh, you add these handy
sod muffs, okay?

1746
01:15:17,480 --> 01:15:18,980
Oh.

1747
01:15:18,980 --> 01:15:20,480
Whoa, all of a sudden
we're at Aqueduct.

1748
01:15:20,980 --> 01:15:22,480
Yeah, you can do
all kinds of stuff.

1749
01:15:22,480 --> 01:15:23,480
Like, uh, take punches.

1750
01:15:23,480 --> 01:15:24,480
-Oh, I'd rather not.
-Not in the mouth.

1751
01:15:24,480 --> 01:15:26,990
I mean-- I mean,
the sound of punches, okay?

1752
01:15:27,490 --> 01:15:29,990
Traditionally, a leather glove
against a heavy metal

1753
01:15:29,990 --> 01:15:31,990
or a heavy punching bag
was used, okay?

1754
01:15:31,990 --> 01:15:32,990
Heavy metal punching bag.

1755
01:15:33,490 --> 01:15:33,990
-Ooh.
-Oh.

1756
01:15:33,990 --> 01:15:36,000
But the sound
in this Ator movie

1757
01:15:35,990 --> 01:15:37,490
is much, much cheesier.

1758
01:15:37,500 --> 01:15:39,500
Right, I'm way
ahead of you, buddy.

1759
01:15:39,500 --> 01:15:41,500
You just use these,
